@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/prediction#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<> a orexis:OntologyGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  OREXIS PREDICTION, AGENT 0.2.0.
#  What the prediction package of Agent 0.2.0 declares: one word. A prediction is the calculation
#  of when a reading changes range — the domain's drifts run over the observation a sensor last
#  made, at the rungs of a ladder that is this package's scan, every crossing of a range bound
#  bisected, and one orexis:PredictionGraph written per stretch between crossings, holding a
#  predicted sosa:Observation with its number. The observation is found by the kernel's kind and
#  SOSA's words, a range is SSN-System's, and which side a stretch is on is a revision the sensing
#  layer's rules conclude of it; nothing of sensing is imported or spoken here.

:Drift a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Drift" ;
    rdfs:comment """What a value does by itself while nobody acts — a pot drying, a barrel draining.
    SOSA has no word for it: a sosa:Procedure is how an observation is MADE, and a drift is how the
    world moves what was observed. A drift carries sh:construct, a rule over the observation in hand
    answering the predicted observation $elapsed seconds past it, landing at $lands. It declares no
    horizon: the ladder it is asked at is the scan's, and the bisection places a crossing wherever it
    falls.""" .
